  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-09">3-tier `IThreadResolver` — subject/conversation thread → per-record default thread (ONE per record, lazy) → per-user master catch-all; add a `default-thread` marker. Every inbound/outbound message resolves to a non-null thread; per-record default created lazily; master is per-user; the policy is a resolver change (no new access path).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project-CRITICAL">This EDITS shared `Services/Communication/ThreadResolver.cs`. Author/run characterization tests pinning the CURRENT email + messaging resolution behavior (Tier-1 JOIN, record-anchored CREATE, SKIP→null, NFR-02 swallow) and confirm GREEN BEFORE extending; keep GREEN after. No historical backfill (point-forward).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024 / ADR-046">Tier 2's per-record default reuses the SAME ADR-024 regarding (`ReadRegardingAnchorAsync`); MUST NOT add a second regarding mechanism. No CommunicationConnections / Field Mapping Framework for the thread anchor.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02">Thread assignment stays best-effort / non-fatal — a resolve/create failure MUST NOT fail the send or inbound-capture path (log + continue; the message still persists, worst case without `sprk_communicationthread`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">The `default-thread` marker is an ADDITIVE field (task 002). MUST NOT retype the existing Text `sprk_regardingrecordtype`; MUST NOT alter existing thread fields.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03 / ADR-028">Write/resolve-side only. MUST NOT touch the impersonation read path, add a second access mechanism, or reintroduce membership-union on reads (retired 2026-07-16).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">If any tier is feature-gated, use the Null-Object kill-switch + symmetric registration; otherwise register unconditionally via the existing `CommunicationModule`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Integration-heavy; characterization tests for the frozen resolver FIRST; unit/seam coverage of all 3 tiers. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;` / DI-registration / ctor-null-check tests; boundary mocks only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`parallel-safe: false` — serializes the W7 shared-resolver edit; never concurrent with 050 or any other BFF writer. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` hot-path).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-§10">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta vs ~46.99 MB baseline (expect ≈0, no new package); no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
