  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `ThreadResolver.cs` (JOIN/CREATE/SKIP branches, `ReadRegardingAnchorAsync`, `CreateThreadAsync`, the NFR-02 swallow), `IThreadResolver.cs`, the per-channel `IThreadKeyStrategy` impls, and both call sites (`IncomingCommunicationProcessor` inbound, `CommunicationService` outbound). Read task 002's `default-thread` marker schema (exact field name + type).</step>
    <step order="2">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F + root §11 Component Justification + ADR-024/ADR-046 (no second regarding mechanism) + ADR-028 (read path untouched) before defining the ladder.</step>
    <step order="3">**CHARACTERIZATION FIRST (shared-code safety gate).** Author/confirm characterization tests pinning CURRENT resolver behavior: (a) Tier-1 JOIN by channel key, (b) record-anchored CREATE, (c) the SKIP→null path (no groupable key), (d) NFR-02 non-fatal swallow. Run them; confirm GREEN. Do NOT edit `ThreadResolver.cs` until these are green. Record the baseline in `current-task.md`.</step>
    <step order="4">Define the Tier-2/Tier-3 helpers: `FindOrCreatePerRecordDefaultAsync(anchor)` (query `sprk_communicationthread` where `default-thread` marker set AND regarding = this record → join, else create + mark) and `FindOrCreatePerUserMasterAsync(ownerId)` (query where `default-thread` marker set AND owner = this user → join, else create + mark). Both lazy + idempotent via the task-002 marker.</step>
    <step order="5">Extend `ResolveAndAssignThreadAsync`: at the current SKIP branch (line ~66), instead of returning null, fall through — if `ReadRegardingAnchorAsync` yields a regarding, use Tier 2 (per-record default); else use Tier 3 (per-user master). Assign the resolved thread. Tier 1 JOIN/CREATE remains first and unchanged.</step>
    <step order="6">Ensure idempotency: Tier 2 creates AT MOST ONE default thread per regarding record (concurrent orphans for the same record must not create duplicates — query-before-create keyed on marker + regarding); Tier 3 AT MOST ONE master per owning user. Document the concurrency assumption in a code comment.</step>
    <step order="7">Keep the whole ladder inside the existing NFR-02 try/catch — a Tier-2/Tier-3 failure logs + returns null (message persists without a thread) rather than throwing to the caller. Confirm the marker write is additive (NFR-04) and touches no existing thread field.</step>
    <step order="8">Confirm DI: the resolver is already registered via `CommunicationModule`; no new registration needed unless a tier is feature-gated (then ADR-032 Null-Object + symmetric registration). State which.</step>
    <step order="9">Write the extension tests: (a) a message with a groupable key still JOINs Tier 1 (unchanged); (b) an orphan WITH a regarding lands in the per-record default; a SECOND orphan for the same record joins the SAME default (lazy + idempotent); (c) an orphan with NO regarding lands in the per-user master; a second such orphan for the same user joins the SAME master; (d) every path returns a non-null thread; (e) a simulated Tier-2/Tier-3 failure is non-fatal (NFR-02). RE-RUN the Step-3 characterization tests — confirm STILL GREEN.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` then `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/msg-r2-070-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~46.99 MB baseline. Expected ≈ 0 (no new package).</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates (REQUIRED — shared-path edit): `code-review` on the diff (focus: Tier-1 behavior preserved, NFR-02 non-fatal, ADR-024/ADR-046 no second mechanism, idempotent lazy creation, §11 justification, read path untouched); `adr-check` against `spec.md`. Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification. Per root §6.5, surface any ADR tension rather than silently complying.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` hot-path — coordinate with 050 which edits the same shared area; they are `parallel-safe: false` and must not overlap). Then update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (070 ✅) + reset `current-task.md`; record decisions (ladder shape, marker field name, lazy-idempotency approach, characterization-test locations).</step>
  </steps>

