  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Every inbound AND outbound message resolves to a NON-NULL thread — Tier 1 (subject/conversation), Tier 2 (per-record default), or Tier 3 (per-user master); each tier is a separately testable case.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tier 2 creates the per-record default thread LAZILY (first orphan for a record creates it) and ONE per record (a second orphan for the same record joins the same default — verified by test, no duplicate).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tier 3 creates the per-user master catch-all ONE per owning user (a second no-regarding orphan for the same user joins the same master — verified by test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The `default-thread` marker (task 002) distinguishes auto-created default/master threads from conversation threads and keys the idempotent find-or-create; the write is additive (NFR-04, no existing field retyped).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">**Existing email + messaging resolution flows continue to pass (characterization tests green)** — Tier-1 JOIN, record-anchored CREATE, and the NFR-02 non-fatal swallow are unchanged before and after; only the former SKIP→null cases now fall through to Tier 2/3.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Assignment is best-effort/non-fatal (NFR-02): a simulated Tier-2/Tier-3 failure does NOT fail send/capture; no second regarding mechanism introduced (ADR-024/ADR-046, grep/diff-verifiable); the impersonation read path is untouched (ADR-028).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; publish-size delta ≈ 0 vs ~46.99 MB; no new HIGH CVE; Step 9.5 gates run; `/conflict-check` clean before PR.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: no historical backfill introduced (point-forward only — pre-existing orphaned messages are NOT reassigned); no new access path / membership-union added; no new NuGet package.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

